  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). PARTLY DONE, PARTLY DUPLICATE. (a) pony actor/primitive: still emitted via pony.py:327, no later pass normalises them, and the validation_report flags both as errors on a live run (3 axis_conformance + 3 id_format); 'actor' duplicates WI-higik, and 'primitive' is moved there. (b) DONE: the sixth producer-emit shape is in the concept-audit playbook (:251-261), though its header at :223 still says 'five'. (c) CURRENT: slice _CONTAINER_KINDS (slice.py:635-638) lacks object, actor, record -- `slice --entry Registry --reverse` on a Kotlin object returns only {Registry:object}; the same code as a class returns members plus main; a Pony actor entry also returns only itself. Drop 'variable': the set drives member expansion through contains edges and a Go variable has no members. (d) type_like_kind_names() correctly omits module/program (kinds that declare a nominal type); the real gap is that there is no anchor-kind predicate. (e) JS class-field initializer anchored on the file (calls app.js(file) -> helper): ADR-0023 now records this as a permitted divergence needing its own measurement before any change -- P4 within this item. Remaining scope: (c), (d), the playbook header; (e) only after measurement. P3 kept."  # 3c6e
